entityDescription:
The Italian Red Cross, also known as CRI, is a non-profit organization, which carries out its mandate and activities in the humanitarian field within the framework of the International Movement of the Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies, of which it is member. The CRI plays a unique role in Italy as an auxiliary to the public powers in the humanitarian field, an institutional role that derives from the Geneva Conventions of which the Italian Republic is a signatory. It is also recognized for its task of protecting health and preventing diseases, responding to emergencies and reducing risks related to disasters and spreading a culture of non-violence and peace, through the promotion of Humanitarian Principles and Values and International Humanitarian Law. The organization of the Italian Red Cross is inspired by the principles of subsidiarity, democracy and electivity of the association offices, of separation between the direction and control functions and the autonomous operational functions of the territorial bodies, as well as the criteria of effectiveness, efficiency and economy. The Italian Red Cross can count on the work of about 160.000 volunteers who are involved in implementing actions to achieve the CRI 2030 Strategic Objectives, which are: 
&bull;Fulfilment of humanitarian mandate of Italian Red Cross through organizational capacity building (organizational development, fund raising, projects&rsquo; monitoring, planning and evaluation, management of human resources).
&bull;Involvement of volunteers and staff in decision-making process (enhancement of voluntary service and promotion of active citizenship with a special focus on youth) 
&bull;Promotion and dissemination of Red Cross/Red Crescent Principles, humanitarian values andInternational Humanitarian Law (advocacy and promotion of a culture of non-violence and peace); 
&bull;Safeguarding and promotion of health and safety education (first aid activities, blood donation, health education and healthy lifestyle promotion); 
&bull;Promotion of social inclusion and integration of vulnerable people (activities aiming at supporting and promoting the inclusion of marginalized people, such as homeless, poor persons, migrants, elderly, people with disabilities, etc.; social support in hospitals, including clown-therapy and psychosocial support); 
&bull;Disaster risk reduction, raising communities resilience through prevention and preparedness in case of disaster (disaster preparedness and response at national and international level; psychosocial support activities in time of crisis; health assistance at major events; mitigation and resilience to climatic changes, etc.); 
&bull;Cooperation with RC Movement and RC National Societies increasing projects and areas of intervention abroad.
